  "llm_summary": "\n\nThe current absence of recent events suggests a period of relative stability, but the live mode requires continuous monitoring of GDelt articles for emerging conflict signals, earthquake data for potential destabilizing natural events, and exchange rate fluctuations indicating economic pressures that may precede unrest. The integration of these diverse sources allows for a multidimensional early-warning framework, though gaps in real-time data could delay detection of nascent threats. Prioritizing rapid analysis of GDelt narratives and economic indicators would enhance responsiveness if tensions arise. Earthquake activity, while less directly linked, could exacerbate existing vulnerabilities in fragile regions. Regular cross-referencing of these datasets is critical to identify convergent risk factors.\n"
